course: dictionary
lesson: 3533
title: One word, many meanings: feature
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning. «Feature» is a good example. The meaning you choose depends on the words around it, which is its context. Read the whole sentence before you decide.
explain: Most of the time, a feature is an important or interesting part or quality of something. «The map shows the main features of the land: rivers, hills and the coast.» Here the features are the natural parts of the land that you can see on the map.
explain: Features can also be the parts of your face, such as eyes, nose and mouth. In a newspaper, a feature is a special article on one topic. In films and games, a feature is a special quality, like a new button or a secret level.
explain: As a verb, to feature means to include or show something important, or to appear in something. «The new film will feature a talking dog» means the film will show a talking dog as an important part. Check your meaning by putting it back into the sentence.
fact: A feature is an important or interesting part or quality of something.
fact: Features are the parts of your face, like eyes, nose and mouth.
fact: In geography, physical features are natural things like rivers, mountains and coasts.
fact: «Newspaper features include a headline, a photo, a caption and columns.» A caption is the words under a photo that help the reader.
fact: To feature means to include or show something important, or to appear in something: «a feature film» is a film with a main story, and «featuring» means with someone important in it.

exercise: «The map shows the main features of the land: rivers, hills and the coast.» What does feature mean here? | The shape of a hat | *Important or natural parts of the land | A tiny drawing in the corner | A film made by the children
exercise: Ravi says features are the parts of your face. Which one is a feature of a face? | *Nose | Cloud | Shoes | Bicycle
exercise: «The newspaper had a feature about the new park, with photos.» What is a feature here? | A hidden coin | A type of bird | A broken machine | *A special article on one topic

test: Which of these is a feature of a newspaper that helps readers? | A puddle | A tent | A sneeze | *A caption under a photo
test: «The new film will feature a talking dog.» What does feature mean here? | To run away fast | To be very small | *To include or show something important | To pack a bag

exam: «Undocumented feature» is a joking name for a software bug. What does feature mean in this phrase? | A type of pencil | To write a report | A place where games are played | *A quality a program has, even a mistake nobody planned
